  "theoryOfChange": "Charity Water utilizes a 'monitoring and evaluation framework' called the MAP Framework to collect data across various water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) indicators. This framework aims to understand the impact of funded projects, maximize effectiveness, and guide future funding priorities. The MAP Framework includes two types of data collection: Annual Check-ins (household surveys) and Post-Implementation Monitoring (comprehensive assessments of past work). Additionally, Charity Water's 'How We Work' page outlines their approach, which involves working with local partners, focusing on rural areas, and a commitment to monitoring, evaluation, and maintenance to ensure sustainable programs. They also articulate 'strategic pillars' that guide their vision, including providing safe drinking water, collaborating with implementing partners, aiming for long-term sustainability, integrating sanitation and hygiene activities, and targeting high-need rural communities.",
